meta {
  name: 45 Apply Center Changes (Assign-Edit Center dialog)
  type: http
  seq: 45
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/accession/transfers/apply-center-changes
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{businessAccessToken}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "changes": [
      { "transferId": "{{transferId}}", "destinationBranchId": "{{branchId}}", "expectedDestinationBranchId": "{{currentBranchId}}" }
    ],
    "retrieveSampleIds": [],
    "sendDate": "2026-10-23",
    "sendTime": "10:00",
    "logisticsType": "Courier",
    "logisticsPerson": "Amit Driver",
    "notes": "Re-addressed from the Edit Center dialog"
  }
}

tests {
  test("applied (or refused as a whole)", function () {
    expect(res.getStatus()).to.be.oneOf([200, 201, 422]);
  });
}

docs {
  The Assign Center / Edit Center dialog's **Confirm** for INTERNAL transfers, as ONE
  all-or-nothing request. Returns `{ changed, retrieved }`.

  Body:
  - `changes[]` - `{ transferId, destinationBranchId }` per ticked tube: each tube carries its
    OWN center, so one request can send different tubes to different branches. A tube whose
    center is unchanged is left out unless the logistics were edited.
  - `retrieveSampleIds[]` - the un-ticked tubes. Each is Retrieved exactly like
    `POST order-samples/:id/retrieve` (back to Accepted, the open INTERNAL transfer is
    soft-deleted - see that request for the audit entries).
  - the shared logistics fields (`sendDate`, `sendTime`, `sampleForm`, `logisticsType`,
    `logisticsPerson`, `notes`, `attachmentUrl`) apply to every changed tube.
  A request with neither `changes` nor `retrieveSampleIds` is refused 422 (nothing to change);
  a tube cannot be both retrieved and re-addressed in the same request; at most 200 entries.

  **All or nothing.** Every change is checked first, then everything is written in one
  transaction (conditional updates, tubes locked in a fixed order, so it is safe against the
  receiving branch pressing Receive at the same moment). If any tube cannot be done, NOTHING
  is changed and the answer is 422 `CENTER_CHANGES_REFUSED` whose message names the tube
  ("Nothing was changed. Tube ACC-...: ...") and whose details carry `accessionNo` and
  `reasonCode` (the error code the single-tube call would have given).

  **Which tubes can be changed.** Only a tube whose INTERNAL transfer is still In-Transit or
  Picked Up. Once the receiving branch has Received / Accepted it, or has sent it back
  (Repeated / Rejected), the tube is refused (the dialog shows it locked).

  🔒 **RBAC (checked per tube in the service; admin roles bypass):** a tube with no center yet
  needs an *Assign* center permission, a tube that already has one needs an *Update* center
  permission (the same groups as `POST transfers/:id/assign-center`); any `retrieveSampleIds`
  needs the Retrieve permission (`accession:in_house_order__retrieve_the_action`).

  Logistics: the receiving branch sees an In-Transit transfer only after a logistics type is
  set (see `32 Transfer - Assign Center`), so Edit Center is also how a logistics type is added later.

  **Re-addressing a transfer the first branch already Picked Up.** Changing the destination of
  an INTERNAL transfer to a DIFFERENT branch while it is Picked Up starts it over: it goes back
  to IN_TRANSIT and the old pick-up (`pickedUpBy` / `pickedUpAt`) is cleared, because the new
  branch has not picked it up (it must Pick Up before it can Receive; the old branch can do
  nothing with it). Every change of destination (also a first assignment) is recorded in the same
  transaction: a row on the sender sample's history (action `assign-center`, "Center changed from
  X to Y while <stage>", plus "it had been picked up, so it starts over at In-Transit" when reset)
  and Audit-log entries (module ACCESSION, `metadata.side`): `sender` under the sending branch
  always; `old-receiver` under the old destination when it had been able to see the transfer (it
  now loses it); `new-receiver` under the new destination once it can see it (an In-Transit
  transfer needs a logistics type first). Saving the same destination again (a logistics-only
  edit) is not a re-address and writes none of this.

  **Stale dialog guard.** Each `changes[]` item may carry `expectedDestinationBranchId`: the
  destination the dialog was showing for that tube (`null` = no center yet). When it is given and
  the tube's destination is no longer that (someone else re-addressed it after the dialog opened),
  the whole request is refused 422 `CENTER_CHANGES_REFUSED` ("Nothing was changed. Tube ACC-...:
  The center of this tube was changed by someone else after this dialog was opened. Close the
  dialog and open it again ...", reasonCode `TRANSFER_CENTER_CHANGED`) and nothing is written. It
  is checked when the request is prepared and again in the write itself (the write is conditional
  on that destination), so a change landing in between is caught too. Omitted = no check (older
  callers). A tube that was Received in the meantime is still reported as not editable.

  **The destination must OFFER every test on the tube (Phase 1).** A tube can only go to a branch that has an
  ACTIVE Lab Test List entry for each of its tests. The match goes through the tenant test both branches copied
  (the sender's Branch Master Data test -> `sourceMasterLabTestId` -> the destination's Branch Master Data test
  with the same tenant test -> an active, not deleted list entry); any of the destination's lists counts. A test
  with no tenant link (hand-created at the branch) cannot be matched and counts as NOT offered. A free-text tube
  test (no catalogue test) is skipped. Otherwise: 422 `DESTINATION_LACKS_TEST`, "<Branch> does not offer: <tests>.
  Choose another branch." (at most five test names, then "and N more"); nothing is changed.
  Checked when the destination CHANGES (first centre or Edit Center), not on a logistics-only save that keeps the
  destination it already had. `apply-center-changes` refuses the whole batch naming the tube
  (`CENTER_CHANGES_REFUSED`, "Nothing was changed. Tube ACC-...: <Branch> does not offer: ...").
}
